frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# The il Cannone violin body at 6 mm, data/instruments/geometry/violin-cannone-guarneri-1743-esrf2026/shell-assembly-h6.tsv
# (64 parts, 11769 nodes, 17483 triangles, 157 ties), the same generator's mesh of the same body as shell-assembly-h8.tsv
# with its one-fan repair (fanfix=move).
# Every choice is h8's (cannone-h8.assembly) but the window and the projection work. Body modes from 15 Hz (above the
# free body's rigid motion) to 5 kHz, the narrower violin shell pack's validity: the spruce pack's source band (Viala's
# model updating, 100-5000 Hz); the maple pack declares Laemmlein's 150 Hz to 10 kHz sweep. No source reaches 5-6 kHz.
window-hz 15 5000
# The owner's conservative bound for 11769 nodes, 128 modes and four bridges is about 7.7e11 terms: 2^40.
projection-work 1099511627776
# The performance body record's thickness [m]; every part's own thickness is written as a ratio to it.
reference-thickness-m 0.003
# Spruce (top, bass bar, soundpost) is the performance body pack, maple (back, ribs, bridge) the other.
pack spruce @body
pack maple violin-maple-sycamore-sonderegger2013-shell.fsmatpk
# Strings G, D, A, E meet the bridge at these points (x, y) [m] of the table (string-contacts.tsv beside it). The table's
# frame has x across the body, so each string drives its bridge node along x, the bowing direction.
bridge-component bridge
bridge-direction 1 0 0
bridge -0.01734 -0.05164
bridge -0.00557 -0.05421
bridge 0.00629 -0.05329
bridge 0.01728 -0.04887
